Subject: [PATCH 02/11] chore(lint): ruff full rule set as a CI gate
 (E,F,W,B,UP,SIM,C90,BLE)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

backend/ruff.toml now selects the Phase 3 rule set from the remediation
plan; `ruff format --check` joins `ruff check` in the backend-lint job.

Real changes made to get to zero:
- 81 `assert False` in tests -> `pytest.fail(...)` (B011).
- admin.py: two helpers and three import blocks moved above the first
  statement (E402); the module still imports cleanly.
- video_job_service: `return` inside `finally` replaced by an
  `if not lease_lost:` guard — a `return` there would have swallowed any
  exception in flight (B012).
- `raise ... from exc` at six sites (B904); `zip(..., strict=False)`
  spelled out (B905); ambiguous `l` renamed (E741); SQLAlchemy `== True`
  -> `.is_(True)` (E712); nested ifs merged; `contextlib.suppress` for
  try/except/pass; f-strings for %-format; `datetime.UTC`.
- 22 functions above complexity 20 carry `# noqa: C901` with the reason
  "Phase 4 split" — the backlog is visible in-tree and cannot grow.
- 144 blind `except Exception` carry `# noqa: BLE001 -- <reason>`; the
  reason is derived from what the handler does (falls back / surfaces the
  error text / degrades Redis / rolls back / skips the item). 31 of them
  are silent `pass` handlers and say so; narrowing them is Phase 4 work.
- UP042 (str+Enum -> StrEnum) is ignored with a reason: it changes
  str()/format() of members and is not a lint-time change.

Verified: ruff check + format clean, `import app.main` ok, 1363 tests.

